Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.089 --> 00:00:01.089
Speaker 1: All right.

00:00:01.089 --> 00:00:02.840
Let's get to the e-mail mailbag for the week.

00:00:02.840 --> 00:00:07.540
If you have something to say and you feel
like it's worth me checking it out, you can

00:00:07.540 --> 00:00:10.000
email info at David Pakman dot com.

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:14.990
Sometimes we will grab a YouTube comment here
or there or a Twitter reply or a Facebook

00:00:14.990 --> 00:00:17.160
post or whatever the case may be.

00:00:17.160 --> 00:00:18.160
But not this week.

00:00:18.160 --> 00:00:23.010
This week it is all bona fide emails, the
first coming from Chris.

00:00:23.010 --> 00:00:29.119
In fact, I received a number of beautiful
messages and some trolling about my COVID

00:00:29.119 --> 00:00:35.520
illness which spread through the house like
a virus which it is.

00:00:35.520 --> 00:00:38.860
Last week Chris said, Sorry to hear about
your COVID illness.

00:00:38.860 --> 00:00:42.129
I hope you get better soon and have no long
COVID effects.

00:00:42.129 --> 00:00:46.360
I got it back in August for the first time
and luckily my sickness wasn't too bad other

00:00:46.360 --> 00:00:48.719
than a headache for a day.

00:00:48.719 --> 00:00:51.880
Thanks for everything you do and I wish you
the best for you and your family.

00:00:51.880 --> 00:00:54.960
Yes, I had it worse than a headache for a
day.

00:00:54.960 --> 00:01:01.219
In fact, there was about a 28 hour period
where I was as sick as I can remember being,

00:01:01.219 --> 00:01:03.449
and I got all sorts of different messages.

00:01:03.449 --> 00:01:08.830
There was someone who wrote to me and said
that they put hydrogen peroxide in their throat.

00:01:08.830 --> 00:01:10.700
Now, why am I saying it that way?

00:01:10.700 --> 00:01:11.780
Because that's the way they wrote it.

00:01:11.780 --> 00:01:14.409
You can see that message on my Twitter and
Instagram.

00:01:14.409 --> 00:01:19.110
They said they put it in their throat and
then something about lemon juice.

00:01:19.110 --> 00:01:20.180
I didn't do that.

00:01:20.180 --> 00:01:23.900
I didn't introduce light and heat inside the
body.

00:01:23.900 --> 00:01:28.860
I didn't use bleach or any of that stuff.

00:01:28.860 --> 00:01:30.660
And fortunately.

00:01:30.660 --> 00:01:32.460
Fortunately.

00:01:32.460 --> 00:01:33.840
It wasn't as bad as it could have been.

00:01:33.840 --> 00:01:36.350
It was pretty bad, but it wasn't as bad as
it could have been.

00:01:36.350 --> 00:01:40.140
And I appreciate all of the messages from
everybody.

00:01:40.140 --> 00:01:46.250
Sharon wrote in about what is a very contentious
topic and about which I have made a decision.

00:01:46.250 --> 00:01:48.310
And I'm going to ask you to respect that decision.

00:01:48.310 --> 00:01:49.860
You don't have to like it.

00:01:49.860 --> 00:01:51.090
But I am going to need you to respect it.

00:01:51.090 --> 00:01:53.710
Sharon wrote in about interruptions.

00:01:53.710 --> 00:01:55.710
And Sharon said, I enjoy watching your show.

00:01:55.710 --> 00:01:58.899
Often Christo evolves, has a YouTube show.

00:01:58.899 --> 00:02:03.740
And when he shows a political clip, we see
only the clip on the screen.

00:02:03.740 --> 00:02:05.399
You don't see my mug.

00:02:05.399 --> 00:02:08.390
And he does not share the screen or interrupt.

00:02:08.390 --> 00:02:12.360
Have you ever gone to see a movie with someone
and they talk or try to get your attention

00:02:12.360 --> 00:02:13.360
during the movie?

00:02:13.360 --> 00:02:14.650
They ruin the movie.

00:02:14.650 --> 00:02:17.860
I lose the joy of the moment when there are
constant interruptions.

00:02:17.860 --> 00:02:20.920
It's nerve wracking and I generally end it
before the show is over.

00:02:20.920 --> 00:02:25.030
I so wish you would not interrupt your clips
or other featured program.

00:02:25.030 --> 00:02:26.310
Thanks, Sharon.

00:02:26.310 --> 00:02:27.890
So listen.

00:02:27.890 --> 00:02:28.890
I get it.

00:02:28.890 --> 00:02:29.890
There's two views on this.

00:02:29.890 --> 00:02:32.050
One is, David, shut up.

00:02:32.050 --> 00:02:33.950
Just play the clip and don't say anything.

00:02:33.950 --> 00:02:34.950
Start to finish.

00:02:34.950 --> 00:02:38.580
The other view is I can get the clip elsewhere.

00:02:38.580 --> 00:02:43.700
The reason I'm watching you, David, is for
your commentary and so manage it the way you

00:02:43.700 --> 00:02:44.700
want to manage it.

00:02:44.700 --> 00:02:49.450
I have made the decision because no matter
what I do, people complain if we just play

00:02:49.450 --> 00:02:51.530
clips, long clips, and I don't say anything.

00:02:51.530 --> 00:02:54.300
A lot of people say it's not even it's like
not even really your show anymore.

00:02:54.300 --> 00:02:56.310
You're just playing a clip.

00:02:56.310 --> 00:03:01.500
I've made the decision, much like during live
streams, where we watch a debate or a rally.

00:03:01.500 --> 00:03:03.480
I will opine.

00:03:03.480 --> 00:03:07.970
I'm trying to offer something in addition
to just being a repeater of clips.

00:03:07.970 --> 00:03:14.190
And so I completely respect people who don't
want to see me or hear from me during clips.

00:03:14.190 --> 00:03:21.780
There are lots of clipping services and Twitter
users who will just post clips and no commentary.

00:03:21.780 --> 00:03:28.310
I've made the decision for the show, for what
the show is, that I will use my discretion

00:03:28.310 --> 00:03:32.750
and sometimes you'll see my face during a
clip and sometimes you will hear me say things

00:03:32.750 --> 00:03:36.170
and I will try to strike the right balance,
as always, with peace and love.

00:03:36.170 --> 00:03:39.840
You know, I will try to strike the right balance
and do everything that everybody wants me

00:03:39.840 --> 00:03:41.950
to do the best possible way.

00:03:41.950 --> 00:03:46.280
But there are going to be interruptions because
that's the format of the show.

00:03:46.280 --> 00:03:51.620
And maybe Christo Evolves has decided on a
different format, and that's a beautiful thing.

00:03:51.620 --> 00:03:56.450
We can all have our formats and we love you
share and that's the important thing.

00:03:56.450 --> 00:04:00.730
We receive the commentary with absolute peace
and love.

00:04:00.730 --> 00:04:04.560
Jason wrote it and said, I think the left
is in trouble.

00:04:04.560 --> 00:04:09.260
Writing with the absolute disaster the Republican
Party has become, more and more people in

00:04:09.260 --> 00:04:11.390
my social circle are voting Democrat.

00:04:11.390 --> 00:04:16.500
Do you believe that as more people move over
to the left, that the left as a whole is in

00:04:16.500 --> 00:04:18.280
danger of becoming more centrist?

00:04:18.280 --> 00:04:22.440
Thanks for taking the time to read the question
and for producing amazing content.

00:04:22.440 --> 00:04:23.810
No, I don't actually.

00:04:23.810 --> 00:04:28.530
I just don't believe that's happening because
there's two things that are taking place here.

00:04:28.530 --> 00:04:32.979
There are people who vote for Democrats.

00:04:32.979 --> 00:04:37.510
Because they love the Democratic platform.

00:04:37.510 --> 00:04:43.260
And there are people who vote for Democrats
because they find it to be the better of the

00:04:43.260 --> 00:04:46.320
two options that have a shot at winning.

00:04:46.320 --> 00:04:53.030
But the truth is that the Democratic electorate
is actually far more to the left of where

00:04:53.030 --> 00:04:55.530
the elected officials are.

00:04:55.530 --> 00:05:01.310
So it's already a very centrist, represented
party.

00:05:01.310 --> 00:05:05.890
And because of a combination of different
factors, including the way districts are drawn

00:05:05.890 --> 00:05:11.380
and so many different things, what I'm actually
seeing is a Democratic Party that, at least

00:05:11.380 --> 00:05:13.900
on paper, has continued to move to the left.

00:05:13.900 --> 00:05:19.610
Now, whether the elected officials move to
the left sort of remains to be seen still.

00:05:19.610 --> 00:05:21.360
But I don't think that that's the case.

00:05:21.360 --> 00:05:28.180
I also think that this is a sort of temporary
aspect where disheartened Republicans who

00:05:28.180 --> 00:05:31.419
don't like MAGA either don't vote or vote
Democrat.

00:05:31.419 --> 00:05:34.039
I think eventually the Democratic Party is
going to figure it out and they're going to

00:05:34.039 --> 00:05:36.070
get away from MAGA and go back to something
else.

00:05:36.070 --> 00:05:38.330
So I don't believe that that's going to be
an issue.

00:05:38.330 --> 00:05:41.440
I think Democrats should take victories while
they can.

